# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# arinzeokigbo.com — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) for local development, and set the same
# keys in the Vercel project's Environment Variables for production.
#
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. Never commit a real value to this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# THE SITE REQUIRES NO ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES.
#
# `NODE_ENV` is the only variable any source file reads, and the framework sets
# it. Everything else is static: the content is committed TypeScript, the social
# card is generated at request time from that content, and there is no database,
# no CMS and no API key.
#
# This file previously declared CONTACT_FORM_SECRET (plus optional
# RESEND_API_KEY / CONTACT_TO_EMAIL / CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL) for a contact
# endpoint at `/api/contact`. Contact is email-only by design — `docs/05` makes
# the address itself the contact section's heading, so it survives a
# headings-only scan — and no form was ever built, so the endpoint was
# unreachable. It has been deleted along with its secret: an unused
# authenticated endpoint is attack surface, and an unset secret that gates it is
# a footgun waiting for someone to set it.
#
# If a form is ever added, restore the endpoint from git history and re-add its
# keys here at the same time — never one without the other.
